      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea that abstaining is a moral act is a dangerous lie that absolves you of your duty to fight for your community's survival. By staying home, you are actively choosing to let corrupt systems fester and grow stronger, which is far worse than voting for imperfect candidates. True moral courage means showing up to disrupt the status quo, even if it means voting for the \"lesser of two evils,\" because your presence alone proves that the people are not dead yet.",
